Core rule

Personality should affect behavior weights, not lock the player out of content.

So instead of:

“This dog cannot make friends.”

Use:

“This dog is less likely to enjoy first meetings, but can still become friends over time.”

This keeps every dog lovable and prevents players from feeling punished for picking a cute dog.

PawFriends Personality System
Recommended personalities

Use 9 personalities:

Personality	Main fantasy
Relaxed	Slow, cozy, loves resting
Gentle	Quiet, obedient, cautious
Energetic	Active, fast, always moving
Loyal	Owner-focused, affectionate
Curious	Sniffs, explores, finds things
Clever	Learns fast, needs variety
Social	Loves dogs and strangers
Playful	Toys, games, park energy
Mischievous	Cute chaos, digging, surprises

This gives enough variety without becoming confusing.

