Map-location effects

Personality should make map locations feel more alive.

Location	Personality bonus examples
Home	Relaxed rests better, Loyal gains more bond from petting
Dog Park	Social, Playful, Energetic get better events
Kennel	Social bonds faster, Gentle gets cautious-friendly interactions
Competition Center	Clever and Energetic perform better
Shop	Curious reacts to new items, Playful reacts to toys
Random street spots	Curious/Mischievous find more presents

Example:

A Curious dog walking through the park might stop to sniff a bush and find a present.
A Social dog in the same spot might instead run toward another dog.
A Relaxed dog might sit down for a short rest animation.

Same route, different personality outcome.

Present system by personality

Presents should not be totally random. Personality can influence what the dog finds.

Personality	More likely to find
Relaxed	Cozy furniture, blankets, cushions
Gentle	Care items, brushes, calm accessories
Energetic	Sport toys, balls, agility items
Loyal	Owner-themed accessories, collars
Curious	Random collectibles, unusual items
Clever	Training items, trick rewards
Social	Gifts after dog encounters
Playful	Toys, plushies, fetch items
Mischievous	Rare junk, surprise boxes, dirty/funny items

This makes item rewards feel connected to the dog.

Dog encounter behavior

When meeting another dog, personality should affect the interaction.

Personality	Encounter style
Relaxed	Calm sniff, may lose interest
Gentle	Shy greeting, slow friendship
Energetic	Excited jump/play, may overwhelm calm dogs
Loyal	Stays near owner, less interested
Curious	Sniffs the other dog and surroundings
Clever	Observes first, reacts based on other dog
Social	Runs up happily, best friendship chance
Playful	Invites play quickly
Mischievous	Teases, barks, playful chaos
Simple compatibility logic

Use personality compatibility for encounter outcomes:

Pairing	Result
Social + almost anyone	High friendship chance
Playful + Energetic	Great play interaction
Gentle + Relaxed	Calm positive interaction
Curious + Clever	Good neutral interaction
Mischievous + Gentle	Lower first-meeting chance
Loyal + Social	Mixed: social dog wants play, loyal dog prefers owner
Energetic + Relaxed	Mixed: one wants movement, one wants calm

This can generate small text like:

“Pepper was curious about Milo.”
“Bella wanted to play, but Luna was a little shy.”
“Rocky and Max became friends quickly!”

Training behavior

Training should not just be “fast/slow.” It should change how the dog likes to learn.

Personality	Training effect
Relaxed	Slower, but low frustration
Gentle	Reliable, fewer mistakes
Energetic	Learns active tricks faster, loses focus if waiting
Loyal	Learns better after petting/praise
Curious	Learns better with variety, worse with repetition
Clever	Fastest learner, but gets bored quickly
Social	Distracted around dogs/visitors
Playful	Learns better through toy rewards
Mischievous	More failed attempts, but special funny animations

This makes training feel personal without making one personality obviously best.

Needs behavior

Keep this subtle.

Personality	Need behavior
Relaxed	Hunger/thirst/activity drain slower
Gentle	Mood stays stable longer
Energetic	Activity drains faster, hunger/thirst faster
Loyal	Attention drains faster
Curious	Boredom rises faster if nothing changes
Clever	Needs mental stimulation
Social	Mood drops faster when alone
Playful	Fun need drops faster
Mischievous	Hygiene drops faster

